   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch6/q6",
   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;-1\\\\7&amp;2\\\\-5&amp;8\\end{pmatrix}\\quad\\mathbf B=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;3&amp;2\\\\-1&amp;6&amp;5\\end{pmatrix}\\quad\\mathbf C=\\begin{pmatrix}-5&amp;2&amp;1\\\\4&amp;3&amp;8\\\\-6&amp;11&amp;2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf I\"></span> is the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\times3\"></span> identity matrix,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>show that there is an integer <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{AB}-3\\mathbf C+k\\mathbf I=\\mathbf 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div>stating the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span></li><li>explain why there can be no constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> such that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{BA}-3\\mathbf C+m\\mathbf I=\\mathbf 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Show how the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf C\"></span> can be used to solve the simultaneous equations<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{gathered}-5x+2y+z=-14\\\\4\\text{x}\\ x+3y+8z=3\\\\-6x+11y+2z=7\\end{gathered}\" data-display=\"true\"></div></li><li>Hence use your calculator to solve these equations.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
