   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch6/q7",
   "question": "<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;-1&amp;1\\\\3&amp;k&amp;4\\\\3&amp;2&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\"></span>&emsp;&emsp;where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> has an inverse. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>, the coordinates of the point where the following planes intersect<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{gathered}2x-y+z=p\\\\3x-6y+4z=1\\\\3x+2y-z=0\\end{gathered}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> for which the set of simultaneous equations<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{gathered}2x-y+z=1\\\\3x-5y+4z=q\\\\3x+2y-z=0\\end{gathered}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>can be solved.</li><li>For this value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>, interpret the solution of the set of simultaneous equations geometrically.</li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
