   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch6/q8",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\"></span> is a 2 by 2 matrix and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf B\"></span> is a 2 by 3 matrix.<br>Giving a reason for your answer, explain whether it is possible to evaluate<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf{AB}\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A+\\mathbf B\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Given that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-5&amp;3&amp;1\\\\a&amp;0&amp;0\\\\b&amp;a&amp;b\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}0&amp;5&amp;0\\\\2&amp;12&amp;-1\\\\-1&amp;-11&amp;3\\end{pmatrix}=\\lambda\\mathbf I\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span> are constants,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>determine<ul><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda\"></span></li><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span></li><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span></li></ul></li><li>Hence deduce the inverse of the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}-5&amp;3&amp;1\\\\a&amp;0&amp;0\\\\b&amp;a&amp;b\\end{pmatrix}\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Given that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}1&amp;1&amp;1\\\\0&amp;\\sin\\theta&amp;\\cos\\theta\\\\0&amp;\\cos2\\theta&amp;\\sin2\\theta\\end{pmatrix}\\qquad\\text{where }0\\leqslant\\theta&lt;\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>determine the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\"></span> for which the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> is singular. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p></li></ol>",
